Ruslan Mirzayev ( [LINK: (Uzbek) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uzbek_language] : Ruslan Mirzayev, Russian: Руслан Мирзаев) (born March 30, 1989) is an  [LINK: (Uzbek) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uzbek_people]  film producer and director. [LINK: ([1]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Random#cite_note-1]  Mirzayev began his film production career in 2011 by shooting the film  [LINK: (Yondiradi Kuydiradi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yondiradi_Kuydiradi_(2011_Uzbek_film)] .


# LIFE #

Ruslan Mirzayev was born on March 30, 1989, in  [LINK: (Gomel) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gomel] ,  [LINK: (Belarus SSR) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Byelorussian_Soviet_Socialist_Republic] ,  [LINK: (Soviet Union) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soviet_Union] . He studied cinematography at the College of Cinema, Video and Technology. After graduating from college, he studied at the  [LINK: (Faculty of Cinematography of the Uzbek State Institute of Arts and Culture) -> https://uz.wikipedia.org/wiki/O%CA%BBzbekiston_davlat_san%CA%BCat_va_madaniyat_instituti] . He began his film production career in 2011 by shooting the film  [LINK: (Yondiradi Kuydiradi) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yondiradi_Kuydiradi_(2011_Uzbek_film)] . [LINK: ([2]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Random#cite_note-2]  He is best known in the movie world through his film Sniper. [LINK: ([3]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Random#cite_note-3]


# CAREER ACTIVITIES #

The collaboration with Turkish filmmakers began with the shooting of Sniper. [LINK: ([4]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Random#cite_note-4]  The film was directed by Ozod Shams and produced by Ruslan Mirzayev, starring Uzbek and Turkish actors. [LINK: ([5]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Random#cite_note-5]  After that, there were rumors on the Internet that a film called My Sun (Güneşim benim) would be shot in collaboration with the Turks, and that the film could receive high ratings. [LINK: ([6]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Random#cite_note-6]  [LINK: ([7]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Random#cite_note-7]  However, shortly afterwards, the film's producer, Ruslan Mirzayev, announced that they had not been able to raise enough money to make the film [LINK: ([8]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Random#cite_note-8]  and began filming the series Battle of the Hearts (Yuraklar jangi) instead. [LINK: ([9]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Random#cite_note-9]  [LINK: ([10]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Random#cite_note-10]  Then, under the leadership of Mirzayev, the team began filming the series Games of Love in collaboration with the screenwriter of the film  [LINK: (Valley of the Wolves) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valley_of_the_Wolves] . [LINK: ([11]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Random#cite_note-11]  After that, Ruslan Mirzayev began working with the Turks on the film Billionaire from Istanbul. [LINK: ([12]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Random#cite_note-12]  [LINK: ([13]) -> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:Random#cite_note-13]


